            <ArticleTitle>Eosinophilia-myalgia syndrome associated with ingestion of L-tryptophan: muscle biopsy findings in 4 patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>319-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Muscle biopsies of 4 patients with the eosinophilia-myalgia syndrome associated with ingestion of L-tryptophan showed lymphocytic infiltrates with occasional eosinophils largely restricted to interstitial fibrous tissue and perivascular areas. There was inflammation and fibrosis of muscle spindle capsules in 3 patients. In the 2 sickest patients, there was profound muscle atrophy, affecting both muscle fiber types.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
